<title>AUSTRIA: Andritz sale lucrative for CA - magazine.</title>
<headline>Andritz sale lucrative for CA - magazine.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austria's Creditanstalt brought in a book profit of over 1.2 billion schillings from selling its 32.8 percent stake in machine factory Andritz AG, news magazine Profil said on Friday.</p>
<p>Creditanstalt sold its stake on March 24 to Andritz's majority shareholder -- German industrial holding company AGIV AG, who now owns 93 percent of Andritz.</p>
<p>The sales price was not disclosed. But Profil, the weekly magazine that goes on sale on Saturday, said sources close to Creditanstalt clearly confirmed the sale brought a book profit of over 1.2 billion schillings for CA.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom, +431 531 12 256</p>
